WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I want to ask
about the book.

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So what made you decide --

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:04.838
Obviously, you're a "New York
Times" best-selling author.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.339 size:75% position:38%
You've never written
a kids book before.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
What brought along
the idea to write this?

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think, for me,
I thought I sort of

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
missed my window
to have children.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.882
I just -- I was busy at work,
and then some other things

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:19.052
happened in life, and sometimes
you think you missed that.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:22.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
And deep inside,
I kind of wished and hoped

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.089 line:92%
and sort of prayed for it.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would scribble
in my journal.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, 'cause I felt like
maybe it would happen,

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:30.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I felt like I loved her
before I held her.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:34.768
Like, I felt like the idea of
her, like, melted me, kind of.

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so that's
where the title came from.

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And have you read it
to her yet?

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:41.107
-I did.
-And how was -- Did she like it?

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, her go-to
is "Good Night Moon,"

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I had to wrestle
that one out of her hand.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:47.347
But when I got this one in,
I was flipping through it,

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
and her eyes
were kind of traveling,

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.117 size:84% position:42%
like from page to page,
so I was digging that.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will say, like, this is --
it's a lot --

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
It has a lot in it that I feel
like my son would dig, too.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:56.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You think?
-'Cause he likes animals.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
He likes to point at things
and see them.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:01.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Yeah. She was chomping
on the elephant page.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.196 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Also, I would love

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:05.231 size:88% position:44%
to get "Good Night Moon"
out of his hands, too.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:08.635
-How are they so hooked on that?
-It's weird.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:09.636 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What is it?

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:13.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's weirdly hypnotic
and strange,

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.607 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and I hate it so much.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.909 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:18.178
There's so many things about it
that I hate so much.

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:21.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, also,
it takes a minute to read it.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:21.881 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's over.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:25.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And when it starts, I'm like,
"Oh, here we go!"

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:28.154 size:75% position:38%
"Oh, let me guess --
mittens and kittens.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:28.655 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh, great."

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.623 size:81% position:41%
But I'm so bummed out,
and I don't know why

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.026
I can't just be an adult
and be like, "Just read."

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:36.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-"It's less than 100 words."

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm so upset reading it,
so I can't.

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm looking forward
to reading this.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:44.938
And then, tell me about,
you got Kelly Clarkson --

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:46.673
-[ Gasps ]
-You played it for me backstage.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
Stunning.
How did you get Kelly Clarkson

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:53.012
to sing the lyrics to your book
that were words.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
They weren't even lyrics.
-You know what?

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.182 line:92%
I asked her if she would do it.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I kind of
felt guilty asking.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said, "You know what?
Let me think about it.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:01.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll try.
I'll let you know.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.857
When you're in Korea,
I'll send you some voice notes."

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.758 size:84% position:42%
So I waited every day,
and I checked my phone,

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I got nothing
from Kelly Clarkson,

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm like, "Oh, God,
she's way too busy.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:09.796 line:92%
I should've never asked."

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:13.266
I got home from it, and I said,
"I'm gonna unhook her

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:14.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
and tell her
don't worry about it."

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was our first guest
on the show when I came back,

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I looked at her,
and I thought,

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:22.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
"She probably feels awkward,
and she goes, "I did it."

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:25.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "You did it?"
She said, "I sang the words.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:26.546 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I hope you like it."

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:30.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
We sat down in the studio,
and she played it.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.684 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And, Seth, I wept.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.154 size:75% position:38%
One, because there's
no one like Kelly.

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:37.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, two, just because
she went to all that trouble.

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:39.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, by the way,
I have to tell you something.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if there's anyone
Kelly Clarkson loves more,

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.364 line:92%
short of her family, than you.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:46.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is --
-And I'm not kidding!

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:49.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, Kelly Clarkson
is so wild about you.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:50.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can I tell you something?
-What?

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:56.209
-I feel the same about her,
and forget about my family.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:57.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because she's --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.844 --> 00:03:00.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She literally finished
this song and said,

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hoda, I gotta go.
I'm on 'Seth' tonight.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.184
We were day drinking last time,
and I don't know

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:05.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
what we're gonna do."
-Yeah.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:08.288
-She's literally so crazy
about you, and I love that.

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:09.589
-She's the greatest person
on Earth, and she should

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.892
do everything, and everybody
should embrace her at all times.

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:14.093 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would be remiss
if I didn't ask.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:18.431
How much Korean did you pick up
on your trip?

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:20.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's really
none of your business.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:20.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:24.771
-I can't remember any of it.
-Can you even remember hello?

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:26.873
-No. God, I can't believe
you're asking me this.

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause I --
-Goodbye? What about --

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:31.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Give me a --
Do you remember any of it?

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:34.280 size:84% position:42%
-Do you know any of it?
-I didn't get to go.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.049 line:92%
Nobody invited me to Korea.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:37.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't --
You know what's funny?

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:40.286
I'm one of those people that --
It's like with anything.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
I learn it.
I know it at the time.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, a week later,
it's gone-zo.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:46.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
-By the way, if all you knew
was hello and goodbye,

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:48.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's not like that's
that impressive, anyway.

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:52.098
Although it's more impressive
than what I'm getting now.

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:53.700 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I cannot remember.
-That's all right.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:58.004
You have a lot on your plate.
You had to write this book.

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:00.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you're right.
All 100 words.

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.508 size:84% position:42%
-So, anyways, thank you
so much for being here.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:03.743
Apologies to our Korean audience
that tuned in

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:04.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
to hear Hoda
say hello and goodbye.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:08.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God! Stop!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:11.150
It's always so great to see you.
-Seth, I love you.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:14.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I love you, too.
Congrats on everything.

